Glutter includes, depends on or is derived from the following components
(docs/SPEC.md section 20).

Flutter framework (BSD-3-Clause)
  The API, algorithms and tests of the Flutter framework are ported to Go.
  Ported files carry "// Flutter:" references.
  Copyright 2014 The Flutter Authors. All rights reserved.
  License text: third_party/flutter/LICENSE

Flutter key data (BSD-3-Clause)
  The generated key tables (physical and logical keys) are derived from
  Flutter's gen_keycodes data (dev/tools/gen_keycodes/data).
  Copyright 2014 The Flutter Authors. All rights reserved.
  License text: third_party/flutter/LICENSE

Flutter's Windows embedder (BSD-3-Clause)
  The keyboard, text input, settings, lifecycle, window and accessibility code of
  internal/platform/windows is ported from the Windows embedder of the Flutter engine
  (engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/windows, and shell/platform/common for the
  accessibility bridge), including the key map (flutter_key_map.g.cc). Ported files carry
  "// Flutter:" references.
  Copyright 2013 The Flutter Authors. All rights reserved.
  License text: third_party/flutter/LICENSE

Chromium accessibility code, as forked in Flutter (BSD-3-Clause)
  The UI Automation provider of internal/platform/windows/uia is ported from the
  accessibility library that Flutter forks from Chromium
  (engine/src/flutter/third_party/accessibility/ax/platform: ax_platform_node_win.cc,
  ax_fragment_root_win.cc, ax_platform_node_textprovider_win.cc and
  ax_platform_node_textrangeprovider_win.cc). The role, action and value tables
  of internal/platform/macos/a11y follow ax_platform_node_mac.mm of the same
  library. Ported code carries "// Flutter:" references to those files.
  Copyright 2015 The Chromium Authors. All rights reserved.
  License text: third_party/chromium/LICENSE

Skia (BSD-3-Clause)
  The Android font configuration parser and the font matcher of
  internal/text/androidfonts are ported from Skia's src/ports/SkFontMgr_android*.
  https://skia.googlesource.com/skia
  Copyright 2011 Google Inc. All rights reserved.
  License text: third_party/skia/LICENSE

SDL 3 (zlib)
  The design of the gpu package and the gamepad, audio and sensor services
  (docs/SPEC.md sections 27 and 28) follows SDL 3's GPU, gamepad, audio and
  sensor APIs. Code ported from SDL 3 (the gamepad mapping parser and table, the
  HID drivers of the pads, the audio resampler and channel conversion, and the
  platform backends of these services) is altered: it is translated to Go and
  changed to fit Glutter, and each ported file says so and names the SDL 3 file
  it comes from. Glutter's identifiers do not use SDL's names.
  https://libsdl.org/
  Copyright (C) 1997-2026 Sam Lantinga <slouken@libsdl.org>
  License text: third_party/sdl/LICENSE

meshoptimizer (MIT)
  The decoders of EXT_meshopt_compression in internal/meshopt (vertex buffers,
  index buffers, index sequences and the vertex filters) are ported from
  meshoptimizer's src/vertexcodec.cpp, src/indexcodec.cpp and
  src/vertexfilter.cpp. The code is translated to Go and changed, and each
  ported file says so and names the meshoptimizer file it comes from.
  https://github.com/zeux/meshoptimizer
  Copyright (c) 2016-2026 Arseny Kapoulkine
  License text: third_party/meshoptimizer/LICENSE

material-color-utilities (Apache-2.0)
  The Material 3 color algorithms are ported from
  https://github.com/material-foundation/material-color-utilities
  Copyright 2021 Google LLC

ebitengine/purego (Apache-2.0)
  Go dependency, used to call C libraries without cgo.
  https://github.com/ebitengine/purego
  Copyright 2022 The Ebitengine Authors

go-text/typesetting (Unlicense OR BSD-3-Clause)
  Go dependency, used for text shaping and layout. Glutter uses a changed copy of v0.3.4 (third_party/typesetting, see its
  GLUTTER.md): the 'gvar' table of a variable font is read one glyph at a time.
  https://github.com/go-text/typesetting

golang.org/x/image (BSD-3-Clause)
  Go dependency, used for WebP and BMP decoding.
  https://pkg.go.dev/golang.org/x/image
  Copyright 2009 The Go Authors

wasm_exec.js of Go (BSD-3-Clause)
  Copied from $(go env GOROOT)/lib/wasm into every web build by glutter-web
  (cmd/glutter-web), so that it matches the Go that built the app.
  https://go.dev/
  Copyright 2018 The Go Authors. All rights reserved.

godbus/dbus/v5 (BSD-2-Clause)
  Go dependency, used for D-Bus.
  https://github.com/godbus/dbus
  Copyright 2013 Georg Reinke, Google

rm4n0s/errors
  Go dependency, used for all error handling.
  https://github.com/rm4n0s/errors

Roboto (SIL Open Font License 1.1) and Material Icons (the license text that
ships with the font in the Flutter SDK: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0)
  Embedded in material/fonts together with their license files
  (Roboto-LICENSE.txt, MaterialIcons-LICENSE.txt). Roboto 3 is from
  https://github.com/googlefonts/roboto-3-classic. The Material Icons font is
  the MaterialIcons-Regular.otf of the font archive that the Flutter SDK
  downloads (https://github.com/flutter/flutter, bin/internal/material_fonts.version);
  its code points are the ones of Flutter's Icons. The pins are in
  material/fonts/VERSIONS.

cupertino_icons (MIT)
  The CupertinoIcons font of the cupertino_icons package (version 2.0.0, from
  https://github.com/flutter/packages, third_party/packages/cupertino_icons) is
  embedded in cupertino/fonts together with its license
  (CupertinoIcons-LICENSE.txt); the code points of cupertino.CupertinoIcons are
  those of Flutter's cupertino/icons.dart. The pin is in cupertino/fonts/VERSIONS.
  Copyright (c) 2016 Vladimir Kharlampidi
  License text: third_party/cupertino_icons/LICENSE

Wayland protocol XML (MIT)
  Kept next to the generated Wayland bindings in
  internal/platform/linux/wayland/protocols, with the licenses of the
  Wayland and wayland-protocols projects.
